# Line endings are normalised to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic. `gofmt -l` reports a file as unformatted when its
# contents differ from gofmt's output, and gofmt emits LF. With Git's default
# Windows checkout behaviour a clone there has CRLF files, so a gofmt check
# fails on every file even though the committed contents are correct. Pinning
# the working tree to LF is what makes the same check pass on Windows, macOS
# and Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell reads either ending, but CRLF is native here and this keeps the
# scripts readable in Windows editors without affecting execution.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Anything binary must never be line-ending converted.
*.exe binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.wasm binary
